1
00:00:24,860 --> 00:00:25,760
YAMU!

2
00:00:26,260 --> 00:00:28,517
YAMU! YAMU! YAMU! YAMU!

3
00:00:28,600 --> 00:00:29,500
YAMU!

4
00:00:30,440 --> 00:00:31,558
You're on the move!

5
00:01:03,840 --> 00:01:08,193
I'd suggest summoning a monster if
you'd like to stay in the game, Joseph.

6
00:01:09,260 --> 00:01:10,640
I can arrange that.

7
00:01:11,040 --> 00:01:13,497
In fact, I'll play five
for the price of one.

8
00:01:13,580 --> 00:01:15,300
Go, Goblin Attack Force!

9
00:01:17,820 --> 00:01:21,660
Now, knock his ancient giant
right out of the ballpark, boys!

10
00:01:22,620 --> 00:01:24,520
Not so fast, Slugger!

11
00:01:24,940 --> 00:01:27,497
Activate Ordeal of a Traveler!

12
00:01:27,580 --> 00:01:30,698
This card is about to make
the game more interesting.

13
00:01:31,340 --> 00:01:35,137
I choose a random card from my hand and
you have to guess whether it's a magic,

14
00:01:35,220 --> 00:01:36,540
trap, or monster card.

15
00:01:36,820 --> 00:01:40,585
If you guess incorrectly, your
monster is returned to your hand.

16
00:01:41,400 --> 00:01:43,500
Guess correctly and you can attack.

17
00:01:43,940 --> 00:01:46,880
So what type of card do I have in my hand?

18
00:01:49,840 --> 00:01:50,720
Let's go.

19
00:01:51,320 --> 00:01:53,560
You've got a one in three chance.

20
00:01:54,740 --> 00:01:57,497
Yugi's grandpa is beating
Joey at his own game.

21
00:01:57,580 --> 00:02:01,097
because he knows joey's strategy
he did teach him how to duel after

22
00:02:01,180 --> 00:02:04,397
all well here it goes it's a trap

23
00:02:04,480 --> 00:02:08,837
card or a magic card it's a monster i

24
00:02:08,920 --> 00:02:13,517
need more time i'm not getting any
younger all right my answer is you're

25
00:02:13,600 --> 00:02:20,260
holding a trap card service heads
monster car that was my next guess

26
00:02:23,720 --> 00:02:28,057
I'm afraid your goblins will have
to wait Now my eyesight's not

27
00:02:28,140 --> 00:02:31,728
what it used to be But it looks
to me like you're defenseless

28
00:02:32,800 --> 00:02:35,800
Nigh in, my turn Sounds good to me

29
00:02:37,420 --> 00:02:42,660
Ah, this should help A little
later, that is But for now,

30
00:02:43,060 --> 00:02:45,460
ancient giant attack him directly

31
00:02:46,620 --> 00:02:47,450
Wrong!

32
00:02:47,600 --> 00:02:48,720
Go, scapegoat!

33
00:02:49,100 --> 00:02:50,000
Activate now!

34
00:02:56,000 --> 00:02:56,960
Nice try!

35
00:02:57,340 --> 00:03:01,380
But I'm safe, so next turn I
can blast you with my goblins!

36
00:03:01,540 --> 00:03:04,775
As usual, you're one step
behind the rest of the class.

37
00:03:05,500 --> 00:03:08,520
See, as long as Ordeal
of a Traveler's in play,

38
00:03:08,800 --> 00:03:12,757
you have to guess my mystery card
every time you want to attack.

39
00:03:12,840 --> 00:03:15,040
What? No way!

40
00:03:15,540 --> 00:03:17,197
Fine, you want to play tough?

41
00:03:17,280 --> 00:03:18,221
I'll play tough!

42
00:03:18,540 --> 00:03:20,481
I already know one of your cards.

43
00:03:21,960 --> 00:03:26,000
All I have to do is get this masked
misfit to play his other card.

44
00:03:26,320 --> 00:03:28,077
Then I'll know it's in his hand.

45
00:03:28,160 --> 00:03:30,940
I activate the card Ancient's Tome!

46
00:03:38,320 --> 00:03:39,150
Awesome!

47
00:03:39,300 --> 00:03:42,241
That means the card left
in his hand is a monster!

48
00:03:43,920 --> 00:03:44,777
By the way,

49
00:03:44,860 --> 00:03:47,397
I assume you know that
Ancient Tome allows me to

50
00:03:47,480 --> 00:03:50,597
switch the card in my hand
with a new one from my deck,

51
00:03:50,680 --> 00:03:51,510
right?

52
00:03:52,980 --> 00:03:54,937
But I had it all figured out!

53
00:03:55,020 --> 00:03:58,537
You'd like to think that, but
old Apnark was way ahead of you.

54
00:03:58,620 --> 00:04:02,500
Now I'll switch my stone giants
to defense mode and end my turn!

55
00:04:10,180 --> 00:04:12,477
Your grandfather just lost 1,000 life

56
00:04:12,560 --> 00:04:14,837
points for not attacking
with his stone giants.

57
00:04:14,920 --> 00:04:16,557
Plus, he switched them into defense mode,

58
00:04:16,640 --> 00:04:19,317
which could cause him to
lose more points next turn.

59
00:04:19,400 --> 00:04:21,282
But that doesn't make any sense!

60
00:04:22,660 --> 00:04:25,780
All right, Pops, it's
go time! Let's do this!

61
00:04:26,480 --> 00:04:28,257
What am I supposed to do now?

62
00:04:28,340 --> 00:04:31,320
Well, I can summon my goblins again,

63
00:04:31,580 --> 00:04:33,977
but as long as he's got
that trap card on the field,

64
00:04:34,060 --> 00:04:36,457
I can't attack unless I
guess what's in his hand.

65
00:04:36,540 --> 00:04:39,128
And these scapegoats
won't last much longer.

66
00:04:39,400 --> 00:04:43,460
In fact, if he draws a monster
next turn, I'm gonna lose the duel.

67
00:04:45,600 --> 00:04:46,697
All right, pal.

68
00:04:46,780 --> 00:04:49,080
Let's try this card again, shall we?

69
00:04:49,540 --> 00:04:51,700
I summon my goblin force!

70
00:04:52,360 --> 00:04:53,940
Care to attack me?

71
00:04:54,280 --> 00:04:55,320
Nope, I'm done.

72
00:04:57,180 --> 00:04:58,100
Thought so!

73
00:04:58,340 --> 00:04:59,987
I guess his strategy worked.

74
00:05:00,240 --> 00:05:03,037
Grandpa Moto has Joey in
the palm of his hand now.

75
00:05:03,120 --> 00:05:05,180
What is Grandpa's strategy anyway?

76
00:05:05,500 --> 00:05:06,559
Do you know, Yugi?

77
00:05:08,560 --> 00:05:11,900
No, but I have a feeling
Professor Hawkins does.

78
00:05:12,260 --> 00:05:15,025
Well, let's just hope
Joey figures it out soon.

79
00:05:19,000 --> 00:05:19,830
No!

80
00:05:22,140 --> 00:05:23,300
I lost.

81
00:05:23,740 --> 00:05:25,622
What time's my next appointment?

82
00:05:25,860 --> 00:05:27,397
It's at 10.30, Doctor.

83
00:05:27,480 --> 00:05:30,440
And the winner is Leon Wilson!

84
00:05:31,180 --> 00:05:32,900
I'd like a second opinion.

85
00:05:35,180 --> 00:05:38,440
I'm hot! I'm hotter! I'm tired!

86
00:05:38,720 --> 00:05:39,760
I'm tireder!

87
00:05:40,060 --> 00:05:41,840
That's not even a word!

88
00:05:45,340 --> 00:05:48,080
Just a few more steps.

89
00:05:51,180 --> 00:05:54,017
I thought this day would never come.

90
00:05:54,100 --> 00:05:57,629
You're the one that said it was
a short stroll to Kaimoland.

91
00:05:57,800 --> 00:05:59,271
That was three weeks ago!

92
00:05:59,660 --> 00:06:01,060
Slight miscalculation.

93
00:06:01,340 --> 00:06:03,977
The important thing is I
was able to get us here.

94
00:06:04,060 --> 00:06:04,890
Right?

95
00:06:04,973 --> 00:06:05,803
Yeah.

96
00:06:05,886 --> 00:06:09,101
Now all we have to do is figure
out a way to enter that tournament.

97
00:06:09,280 --> 00:06:10,110
Don't worry.

98
00:06:10,240 --> 00:06:12,237
I've got a few ideas up my sleeve.

99
00:06:12,320 --> 00:06:13,680
That's what worries me.

100
00:06:14,960 --> 00:06:18,240
You know, for some reason I
feel like we've met before.

101
00:06:18,900 --> 00:06:20,817
Actually, I get that a lot.

102
00:06:20,900 --> 00:06:22,700
But enough small talk.

103
00:06:23,060 --> 00:06:25,397
In order to keep my
ancient tome on the field,

104
00:06:25,480 --> 00:06:28,539
I need to send my sinister
serpent to the graveyard.

105
00:06:28,640 --> 00:06:31,140
This activates my card's special ability,

106
00:06:31,420 --> 00:06:35,357
allowing it to immediately return
to my hand with no questions asked.

107
00:06:35,440 --> 00:06:38,217
In case I'm going too quickly
for you, let me simplify.

108
00:06:38,300 --> 00:06:41,771
My magic card is safe and I
didn't have to give up a thing!

109
00:06:41,920 --> 00:06:43,700
I've had about enough of you!

110
00:06:43,840 --> 00:06:44,957
Sick of me already?

111
00:06:45,040 --> 00:06:48,216
But I haven't even unleashed
my most devastating card!

112
00:06:48,300 --> 00:06:49,420
What would that be?

113
00:06:50,080 --> 00:06:51,297
My prized possession.

114
00:06:51,380 --> 00:06:52,680
My pride and glory.

115
00:06:53,080 --> 00:06:56,517
The thing I've been preparing
for since I played my first card.

116
00:06:56,600 --> 00:06:57,430
Huh?

117
00:06:57,513 --> 00:06:58,808
What are you talking about?

118
00:06:59,360 --> 00:07:01,757
Locked away in the ancient city behind me

119
00:07:01,840 --> 00:07:04,640
lies a powerful creature
known only in legend.

120
00:07:05,080 --> 00:07:06,680
And I will set it free.

121
00:07:07,260 --> 00:07:09,084
Wake me when story time's done.

122
00:07:09,220 --> 00:07:13,220
Every card I've played is an element
needed to let loose this beast.

123
00:07:13,340 --> 00:07:15,200
Only a few steps remain.

124
00:07:16,020 --> 00:07:19,720
First, I move my two stone
giants back into attack mode.

125
00:07:23,540 --> 00:07:27,540
Every move he makes must get him
closer to unlocking that door.

126
00:07:28,840 --> 00:07:32,360
Next, I'll activate the
magic card, Ancient Key.

127
00:07:33,940 --> 00:07:36,140
The ritual is almost complete.

128
00:07:36,660 --> 00:07:39,600
Next, I'll use the
power of my Ancient Key,

129
00:07:39,900 --> 00:07:46,780
along with my stone giants and my Ancient
Tome, in order to unlock the Ancient Gate.

130
00:07:55,480 --> 00:07:57,220
What's behind that?

131
00:07:57,500 --> 00:08:01,520
You're about to find out as
I complete the final step.

132
00:08:01,880 --> 00:08:04,320
I sacrifice my Ancient Gate,

133
00:08:04,760 --> 00:08:11,377
my Ancient Giant, and my Ancient Tome in
order to bring forth my ultimate monster.

134
00:08:11,460 --> 00:08:13,140
No!

135
00:08:13,400 --> 00:08:16,180
Ancient dragon! Arise!

136
00:08:17,760 --> 00:08:19,260
No way!

137
00:08:34,420 --> 00:08:36,220
It's breathtaking.

138
00:08:36,560 --> 00:08:37,677
Could've fooled me.

139
00:08:37,760 --> 00:08:38,817
Check it out.

140
00:08:38,900 --> 00:08:41,680
So that's what he's
been waiting to summon.

141
00:08:42,300 --> 00:08:43,300
It's awesome!

142
00:08:44,040 --> 00:08:47,687
For once, it looks like Joseph
Wheeler is at a loss for words.

143
00:08:47,960 --> 00:08:50,019
I should enjoy this while it lasts.

144
00:08:50,340 --> 00:08:54,400
You know, Yu-Gi, your grandfather's
not the only one with that card.

145
00:08:54,920 --> 00:08:55,750
Huh?

146
00:08:58,040 --> 00:09:00,280
You have an ancient dragon, too!

147
00:09:01,120 --> 00:09:01,950
Yes,

148
00:09:02,033 --> 00:09:04,137
but I've never been able
to summon it because

149
00:09:04,220 --> 00:09:06,691
I don't have all the necessary components.

150
00:09:06,840 --> 00:09:07,720
In fact,

151
00:09:08,020 --> 00:09:11,357
your grandfather is the only
duelist I know who possesses

152
00:09:11,440 --> 00:09:14,417
all seven cards needed to call
forth this divine creature.

153
00:09:14,500 --> 00:09:18,441
So I hope you kids appreciate the
rare event you've just witnessed.

154
00:09:19,460 --> 00:09:23,937
Over the past few years, we've been
involved in a friendly competition of sorts,

155
00:09:24,020 --> 00:09:26,020
both hunting down the same cards.

156
00:09:26,200 --> 00:09:30,820
Until recently, each of us had in our
possession six of the seven cards.

157
00:09:31,000 --> 00:09:32,457
But that would soon change.

158
00:09:32,540 --> 00:09:37,520
Oh, and, uh, by the way, Arthur, I
have some interesting news to report.

159
00:09:37,900 --> 00:09:40,780
Looks like you owe me a chocolate shake,

160
00:09:40,960 --> 00:09:43,820
cause I managed to track
down the fifth card.

161
00:09:44,300 --> 00:09:45,460
You did what?

162
00:09:45,780 --> 00:09:48,580
Now I can finally summon
the ancient dragon.

163
00:09:48,940 --> 00:09:51,140
I must see it. Of course.

164
00:09:51,560 --> 00:09:52,680
Yes, but when?

165
00:09:53,620 --> 00:09:54,502
Did you forget?

166
00:09:54,900 --> 00:09:56,297
I've joined Kaiba's tournament.

167
00:09:56,380 --> 00:09:58,733
What better way to show off my new card?

168
00:09:59,180 --> 00:10:02,240
That was the cheeriest I'd
heard him in a long time.

169
00:10:02,940 --> 00:10:03,770
It was?

170
00:10:03,880 --> 00:10:06,940
Yes, your grandfather is
happiest when he's dueling.

171
00:10:07,540 --> 00:10:09,128
I think it keeps him young.

172
00:10:09,580 --> 00:10:12,720
I guess he's just a
kid at heart. Guess so.

173
00:10:12,960 --> 00:10:14,120
Just look at him.

174
00:10:14,340 --> 00:10:17,777
He's managed to summon a card he's
been waiting to play for years.

175
00:10:17,860 --> 00:10:20,620
And he's about to use it to win this duel.

176
00:10:22,260 --> 00:10:26,340
You should consider it an honor to
be attacked by my ancient dragon.

177
00:10:27,260 --> 00:10:30,617
You spent the entire duel
setting up for one card.

178
00:10:30,700 --> 00:10:33,560
If you ask me, that's
a huge waste of time.

179
00:10:33,820 --> 00:10:34,820
I'm disappointed.

180
00:10:35,140 --> 00:10:37,917
You seem to have forgotten
everything I taught you.

181
00:10:38,000 --> 00:10:38,830
Eh?

182
00:10:38,913 --> 00:10:42,738
Well, suit yourself, because either
way, you're about to be wiped out.

183
00:10:42,860 --> 00:10:47,620
Ancient dragon, destroy his goblin
attack force with legendary blades!

184
00:10:53,140 --> 00:10:54,080
No way!

185
00:10:54,460 --> 00:10:56,257
What happened to my scapegoats?

186
00:10:56,340 --> 00:10:59,317
I see my dragon's special
ability threw you for a loop.

187
00:10:59,400 --> 00:11:02,400
Whenever it defeats one of
your monsters in battle,

188
00:11:02,500 --> 00:11:07,206
it also destroys every monster that's in
defense mode on your side of the field.

189
00:11:07,320 --> 00:11:08,400
That's not cool.

190
00:11:14,520 --> 00:11:16,200
I'll never let you win.

191
00:11:16,480 --> 00:11:20,774
This tournament is my chance to finally
make it big and get some respect.

192
00:11:20,940 --> 00:11:22,460
Like Yugi gets.

193
00:11:23,040 --> 00:11:24,800
I gotta be number one.

194
00:11:25,580 --> 00:11:26,460
I gotta.

195
00:11:26,900 --> 00:11:29,140
Joey, try to lighten up a little bit.

196
00:11:29,400 --> 00:11:32,837
You're so caught up in winning the
duel, you forgot what's important.

197
00:11:32,920 --> 00:11:34,960
You forgot to have fun. Fun?

198
00:11:35,220 --> 00:11:37,880
This is serious, Yook. Chill out.

199
00:11:38,140 --> 00:11:39,905
This tournament's no big deal.

200
00:11:40,080 --> 00:11:43,551
It's just a cheap way for Kaiba
Corp to get some publicity.

201
00:11:43,760 --> 00:11:46,701
You realize I'm standing
right next to you, right?

202
00:11:46,900 --> 00:11:50,940
Just be yourself out there.
Got it? Thanks, guys.

203
00:11:53,940 --> 00:11:55,840
You kids are so supportive.

204
00:11:56,120 --> 00:11:57,757
I'm so proud of you all.

205
00:11:57,840 --> 00:11:59,160
You're proud?

206
00:11:59,380 --> 00:12:01,439
What are you talking about, Hapnog?

207
00:12:03,040 --> 00:12:04,540
Now back to the door!

208
00:12:04,720 --> 00:12:09,360
And from now on, you're not gonna be
the only one having fun, tough guy!

209
00:12:09,840 --> 00:12:11,480
Alright, that's the spirit!

210
00:12:11,700 --> 00:12:15,220
Who cares if Hapnog is more
skilled than you? So what?

211
00:12:15,500 --> 00:12:17,397
Sure, he'll probably win, but...

212
00:12:17,480 --> 00:12:19,100
That's enough motivation!

213
00:12:20,000 --> 00:12:21,020
I'm waiting!

214
00:12:21,960 --> 00:12:24,720
Alright, you wanna see some mad skills?

215
00:12:25,200 --> 00:12:26,320
Bring it on, kid!

216
00:12:26,940 --> 00:12:27,817
Here goes!

217
00:12:27,900 --> 00:12:28,760
Look out!

218
00:12:30,600 --> 00:12:35,340
Time to give my luck one more shot
with a magic card called Roll of Fate!

219
00:12:38,460 --> 00:12:43,700
This card allows me to draw up to six new
cards depending on what number I roll.

220
00:12:43,940 --> 00:12:47,705
Just as long as I remove the same
number of cards from the game.

221
00:12:49,140 --> 00:12:52,680
Now, legendary gambler,
cancel out his roll!

222
00:12:55,580 --> 00:12:59,397
wheeler gets a four and
the freak in the mask gets

223
00:12:59,480 --> 00:13:03,840
a three he shoots he
scores he draws four cards

224
00:13:06,400 --> 00:13:10,457
that's what i call a hand
please tell me you're bluffing

225
00:13:10,540 --> 00:13:15,337
you're about to find out pal
i activate land star forces

226
00:13:15,420 --> 00:13:18,957
this card lets me automatically
summon every land star

227
00:13:19,040 --> 00:13:21,917
monster i'm I'm holding it in
my hand directly to the field.

228
00:13:22,000 --> 00:13:23,780
No questions asked!

229
00:13:26,140 --> 00:13:27,375
And what do you know?

230
00:13:27,700 --> 00:13:30,000
I happen to have three!

231
00:13:35,900 --> 00:13:39,140
And now I'll sacrifice my three Landstars!

232
00:13:39,960 --> 00:13:41,677
This lets me summon...

233
00:13:41,760 --> 00:13:43,220
Guilford the Lightning!

234
00:13:50,060 --> 00:13:51,480
What's going on?

235
00:13:51,880 --> 00:13:56,480
By sacrificing my three land stars, I
activated Guilford's special ability.

236
00:13:56,740 --> 00:14:00,420
So all your monsters are Garners.

237
00:14:01,940 --> 00:14:03,280
Not my dragon.

238
00:14:03,560 --> 00:14:05,220
What a remarkable display.

239
00:14:05,780 --> 00:14:07,760
And I'm just getting warmed up.

240
00:14:08,100 --> 00:14:10,440
Now attack him directly, Guilford.

241
00:14:10,640 --> 00:14:13,287
You'll have to guess
what card this is first.

242
00:14:13,480 --> 00:14:16,420
I've been paying attention,
so don't be so smug.

243
00:14:16,760 --> 00:14:18,617
That, sir, is a monster card.

244
00:14:18,700 --> 00:14:21,400
More specifically, Sinister Serpent.

245
00:14:21,660 --> 00:14:22,860
Well done, Joseph.

246
00:14:24,000 --> 00:14:26,520
Now where was I? Aw, yeah.

247
00:14:26,860 --> 00:14:29,036
Guildford attack that masked man now.

248
00:14:35,740 --> 00:14:37,280
That'll do for now.

249
00:14:39,240 --> 00:14:40,070
Eh?

250
00:14:41,860 --> 00:14:44,660
Your dragon's back. But how?

251
00:14:44,940 --> 00:14:45,820
Quite simple.

252
00:14:46,140 --> 00:14:48,097
My ancient city is still in play.

253
00:14:48,180 --> 00:14:51,140
And as long as that card
remains on the field,

254
00:14:51,380 --> 00:14:54,537
I can continue to bring my
dragon back from the graveyard.

255
00:14:54,620 --> 00:14:56,620
You might say it's indestructible.

256
00:14:56,820 --> 00:15:01,408
You should have known a monster this
special can't be gotten rid of so easily.

257
00:15:01,700 --> 00:15:02,940
We'll see, pal.

258
00:15:03,280 --> 00:15:04,420
Now make your move.

259
00:15:04,640 --> 00:15:06,080
Don't mind if I do.

260
00:15:07,380 --> 00:15:10,420
Now, ancient dragon, attack
Gilbert the Lightning.

261
00:15:12,360 --> 00:15:14,800
Their monster's attack points are equal.

262
00:15:15,140 --> 00:15:16,877
Then they'll both be wiped out.

263
00:15:16,960 --> 00:15:21,200
But not for long, because
that dragon comes back!

264
00:15:28,300 --> 00:15:30,700
Oh, man, not my Guildford!

265
00:15:33,940 --> 00:15:38,960
Not only is your best card
gone, my best card's back!

266
00:15:41,860 --> 00:15:44,200
The odds are against you.

267
00:15:46,960 --> 00:15:50,340
That may be, but my
cards never let me down.

268
00:15:51,220 --> 00:15:52,137
Come on, Deck!

269
00:15:52,220 --> 00:15:53,120
Let's rock!

270
00:15:55,700 --> 00:15:59,080
First, I'll play a magic
card known as Pot of Breed.

271
00:15:59,220 --> 00:16:00,940
So I draw two cards.

272
00:16:07,600 --> 00:16:09,680
I just drew Giant True Name.

273
00:16:09,940 --> 00:16:12,417
That sends every magic
and trap card on both

274
00:16:12,500 --> 00:16:14,657
sides of the field back
to the player's hands.

275
00:16:14,740 --> 00:16:17,677
so I can use it to get
rid of his ancient city

276
00:16:17,760 --> 00:16:20,466
and prevent him from
bringing back his dragon.

277
00:16:21,300 --> 00:16:22,130
Hold on.

278
00:16:22,213 --> 00:16:26,160
Giant True Nate also sends my magic
and trap cards back to my hand.

279
00:16:27,180 --> 00:16:29,900
I can't believe I'm about to say this.

280
00:16:30,220 --> 00:16:32,640
But you're thinking about it too much.

281
00:16:33,200 --> 00:16:35,024
Keep your comments to yourself.

282
00:16:35,480 --> 00:16:38,417
I may not have a deck full
of rare cards like yours,

283
00:16:38,500 --> 00:16:42,237
and I may not plan out my
strategy step by step like you do,

284
00:16:42,320 --> 00:16:45,017
But I think pretty quickly on my feet,

285
00:16:45,100 --> 00:16:47,865
and I always trust my
instincts no matter what.

286
00:16:48,220 --> 00:16:51,044
I guess that's because I
had some good teachers.

287
00:16:51,240 --> 00:16:52,299
Thank you, Joseph.

288
00:16:52,520 --> 00:16:54,100
Er, I mean, good for you.

289
00:16:54,940 --> 00:16:59,587
Yeah, I was taught to play the game with
heart, and above all, always have fun.

290
00:17:00,620 --> 00:17:02,444
And that's just what I'm doing.

291
00:17:02,720 --> 00:17:03,838
Are you ready, pal?

292
00:17:04,260 --> 00:17:05,220
Fire away.

293
00:17:05,600 --> 00:17:09,857
The first thing I'm gonna do is
activate my premature burial magic card.

294
00:17:09,940 --> 00:17:12,897
All I have to do is
give up 800 life points

295
00:17:12,980 --> 00:17:15,517
to bring one monster
back from my graveyard.

296
00:17:15,600 --> 00:17:18,100
And I choose my Goblin Attack Force.

297
00:17:19,660 --> 00:17:23,440
Then I'll activate another magic
card called Giant True Name.

298
00:17:27,080 --> 00:17:28,060
Oh, no!

299
00:17:28,420 --> 00:17:31,900
Now all our magic and trap
cards return to our hands.

300
00:17:36,940 --> 00:17:38,160
My city!

301
00:17:38,760 --> 00:17:42,172
Without that, I have nothing
to protect my ancient dragon!

302
00:17:45,500 --> 00:17:46,940
Inconceivable! Awesome!

303
00:17:47,360 --> 00:17:51,677
If he doesn't screw this up, Joey may
actually have a shot at winning this duel!

304
00:17:51,760 --> 00:17:54,357
I'm afraid there's more
where that came from.

305
00:17:54,440 --> 00:17:59,680
Now that premature burial's back in my
hand, I can activate it again! Oh, boy.

306
00:17:59,960 --> 00:18:02,901
That means Guilford the
Lightning comes back, too!

307
00:18:05,200 --> 00:18:07,197
All right, Guilford! Attack!

308
00:18:07,280 --> 00:18:09,900
Slice and dice his ancient dragon!

309
00:18:19,880 --> 00:18:21,440
I'm wide open!

310
00:18:22,600 --> 00:18:23,430
That's right!

311
00:18:23,513 --> 00:18:24,720
Any last requests?

312
00:18:30,300 --> 00:18:31,920
Did Joey just win?

313
00:18:32,220 --> 00:18:33,780
It would appear he did.

314
00:18:34,140 --> 00:18:35,460
I don't know how.

315
00:18:37,580 --> 00:18:39,060
Nice duel, Stranger.

316
00:18:39,420 --> 00:18:41,560
I just wish I knew who you were.

317
00:18:44,960 --> 00:18:46,657
Actually, you already do.

318
00:18:46,740 --> 00:18:47,580
Hicka-boo!

319
00:18:48,180 --> 00:18:49,010
No way!

320
00:18:50,220 --> 00:18:51,050
Way?

321
00:18:51,133 --> 00:18:52,380
Pretty good disguise, huh?

322
00:18:52,760 --> 00:18:54,360
That could be my new look.

323
00:18:57,220 --> 00:18:59,097
There's something I don't get, Mr.

324
00:18:59,180 --> 00:19:00,010
Moto.

325
00:19:00,093 --> 00:19:02,261
Why'd you join this
tournament in the first place?

326
00:19:03,860 --> 00:19:05,360
You should be resting.

327
00:19:06,000 --> 00:19:09,800
Tell you the truth, I was
hoping to duel you. Why me?

328
00:19:11,080 --> 00:19:15,780
I did teach you everything I know, so I
thought it was about time to test you.

329
00:19:16,380 --> 00:19:17,380
Hmm. And?

330
00:19:17,600 --> 00:19:19,940
Did I pass or what? Let's see.

331
00:19:20,260 --> 00:19:22,940
If I had to grade your duel, you'd get...

332
00:19:23,920 --> 00:19:24,750
A+.

333
00:19:25,600 --> 00:19:26,430
Yes!

334
00:19:26,513 --> 00:19:27,720
I aced the test!

335
00:19:27,940 --> 00:19:30,617
Well, I guess there's a
first time for everything.

336
00:19:30,700 --> 00:19:32,876
Pinch me, because I must be dreaming.

337
00:19:33,320 --> 00:19:35,580
Hey, it's a figure speech.

338
00:19:36,620 --> 00:19:38,500
What a way to kick things off.

339
00:19:39,560 --> 00:19:41,619
Your grandfather dueled quite well.

340
00:19:42,040 --> 00:19:43,397
Yeah, and you know what else?

341
00:19:43,480 --> 00:19:45,598
I think he had more fun than anyone.

342
00:19:45,780 --> 00:19:47,800
So why'd you pick the name Apnog?

343
00:19:47,960 --> 00:19:49,980
It's Grandpa's head backwards.

344
00:19:51,800 --> 00:19:52,760
I don't get it.
